    '|b||Nozick asks how you got what you hold. Rawls asks something earlier: who wrote the rules that decided where you started?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||His test: choose a society''s rules behind a veil of ignorance. You don''t know if you''ll be rich or poor, talented or not, born here or there.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1hw3jyq'
    '|b||So here are three societies, each split into a poorest, a middle and a richest third. The incomes are illustrative.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:8040tj'
    '|b||A is a free-for-all: ten, fifty, a hundred and fifty. B has a safety net: twenty-two, forty-five, a hundred and ten. C is compressed: twenty-five, thirty, forty.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:16beff0'
    '|b||You''ll land in one of those bars at random. Which society do you choose? Behind the veil, which society do you pick?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kn4yhd'
    '|b||Keep your pick, and see whose reasoning it matches.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Rawls chooses C. Behind the veil, guard against the worst: pick the society whose poorest do best.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||But C isn''t equal either.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:i6tvzc'
    '|b||Right, and that''s his difference principle: inequality is just only if it makes the worst-off better off than they''d otherwise be.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:urskks'
    '|a||Nozick wouldn''t play this game at all. But I''ll push back the way the economist John Harsanyi did: you''re equally likely to be anyone, so pick the highest average. That''s A, at seventy.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:g8m1bz'
    '|b||And take a one-in-three chance of living on ten? Rawls thought nobody would gamble a whole life on that.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1jnxqbd'
    '|a||Then here''s the dial between us: the floor you insist on. Societies whose poorest fall below it are out; of the rest, take the highest average.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:962asl'
    '|a||At zero it''s Harsanyi, and A wins. Raise the floor to fifteen and A is out: B wins. At twenty-five, only C is left. That''s Rawls.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:y7na5a'
    '|a||Just above ten. Anyone who wants any floor at all above ten has already left Harsanyi.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So the dial runs from Harsanyi''s average to Rawls''s floor. What do real people choose when you build them a veil?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Norman Frohlich, Joe Oppenheimer and Cheryl Eavey tried it in 1987. Students chose a rule for paying their group before they knew their own income.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:9d05zh'
    '|a||Rawls''s maximin came last. The clear favourite was in the middle: the highest average, with a floor.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ebap5j'
    '|b||Fair enough, people don''t pick my rule. But they didn''t pick your pure average either. And what people choose isn''t the same as what is just.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:l43y6y'
    '|b||Now your side''s problem. Nozick''s test needs a fair start, and real holdings trace back through conquest, slavery and seized land.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:g7sbxg'
    '|a||He admitted it: past injustice might call for a bigger state, for a while, to put things right.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:pjnx0l'
    '|b||And luck is huge. Branko Milanovic found that two things nobody chooses, your country and how it shares its income, account for more than half of income differences across the world.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:7dh9xk'
    '|a||Nozick''s reply: arbitrary or not, your talents are yours, and so is what others freely pay for them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ht7n4c'
    '|a||So how sure are we? That free exchange upsets any pattern: consensus. Which test of fairness is right: contested. That''s a question of values, and no figure settles it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:70abd0'
    '|b||What the figure can do is make you say which you believe: does history decide, or the rules you''d choose blind?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:sblcml'
    '|b||Want the three rules as formulas? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1gao22r'
    '|a||Rawls: of everyone''s income y, make the smallest as large as possible.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Harsanyi: make the average as large as possible.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:73vdat'
    '|a||The lab''s choice: the largest average, among the societies whose smallest y clears the floor.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:x9sqj1'
    '|a||Four new cases. Land was seized from its owners a century ago, then sold on in fair, voluntary sales ever since. By Nozick''s test, is today''s owner''s title just?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:xh69kl'
    '|a||No: the chain starts with a theft. Nozick''s test runs back through the whole history, so rectification is owed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||The chain starts with a theft. Nozick''s test runs back through the whole history, so rectification is owed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Two new societies, X and Y: their poorest and their average.':
